    "problemStatement": "A file system starts at the main folder. You are given a sequence of folder operations: \"../\" : Move to the parent folder (if already at the main folder, stay there). \"./\" : Stay in the current folder. \"x/\" : Move into a child folder named x. Determine the minimum number of operations needed to return to the main folder after performing all operations.",
